# Brief: scratch-copy-removal

## What
Reconcile removes the scratch worktrees a finished run leaves in the worktree store: `verify-*` copies whose run ended or whose owner died, `batch-*` build copies whose builder died, and delegated worker copies `<slug>-u<N>` once their owner leaf merged, using `git worktree remove --force`. `buildStack` writes an owner record before it creates its copy so a running build is never taken.

## Why
Tamdoma/akrogon#93: on 2026-10-15 framework's store held 13 GB in nine leftover copies, kept as "unreachable commits" because the leaf was rebased onto main. These copies are scratch space; crash cleanup should do what the normal path already does.

## Done-criteria
1. A `verify-*` copy whose verify run was killed, at a commit no branch reaches after its leaf was rebased, is gone after the next reconcile pass.
2. A `verify-*` copy whose run is still open with a live owner stays after a reconcile pass.
3. A build paused after its owner record and copy exist survives a second merge pass plus a reconcile pass; once its builder is killed, the next reconcile pass removes the `batch-*` copy and its owner record.
4. A `batch-*` copy with no owner record is removed by a reconcile pass.
5. A `<slug>-u<N>` copy holding a commit not on main and an untracked `__pycache__/` is gone after a reconcile pass once its owner leaf is `merged`; with the owner `failed` it stays under today's guard and is recorded with that guard's reason (`unreachable commits` here). (C)
6. A leaf whose own slug ends in `-u<N>` is handled as that leaf, not as another leaf's worker.
7. None of these copies is removed while a live herdr pane sits inside it, or in a pass where the pane list is unavailable.
8. A dead `verify-*` copy in which a surviving process of this user has its cwd or an open file stays, recorded with that pid as the reason. (B)
9. A `verify-*` copy with no verify record is removed like one whose owner is dead. (C)
/home/ivan/Work/infra/akrogon/issues/open/worktree-cleanup/kept-status/brief.md
# Brief: kept-status

## What
Plain `akrogon status` prints, per registered repo, each path the last cleanup kept and its reason, also for repos with no open leaves, only for paths that still exist, labelled as the last cleanup's result. A merged leaf's own worktree with uncommitted changes stays and is shown that way.

## Why
Tamdoma/akrogon#93: kept worktrees were invisible unless the operator ran `akrogon status <slug>`, so 13 GB sat unseen.

## Done-criteria
1. In a repo with no open leaves and one kept entry whose path exists, plain `akrogon status` prints that path and its reason under the repo, labelled as the last cleanup's result.
2. A kept entry whose path no longer exists is not printed.
3. Plain `akrogon status` changes nothing on disk: the kept entry, its path and the report file are unchanged after it runs.
4. A merged leaf's own worktree with uncommitted changes is still on disk after a reconcile pass and shows in plain status with reason `uncommitted changes`.
/home/ivan/Work/infra/akrogon/issues/open/worktree-cleanup/finished-leaf-processes/brief.md
# Brief: finished-leaf-processes

## What
Reconcile stops the leaf slice of a leaf that is `merged` or `failed` and whose tab is gone, so processes it left running end. Guard units are collected by systemd when they fail, and failed `akrogon-run-*` units already loaded are cleared.

## Why
Store-hygiene F4: a merged leaf's background loop ran 4 h 43 min in its slice after its tab closed, with its folders deleted; 51 finished-leaf slices and 22 failed guard units stay loaded. Leftover processes also block folder cleanup.

## Done-criteria
1. A process left running in the slice of a `merged` leaf whose tab is gone and whose slice holds no live run record is gone after the next reconcile pass, and the slice is inactive; the same holds for a `failed` leaf. (C)
2. The slice of a leaf whose tab is live, or that a live admission record names (an `akrogon verify` or `run-check` started from a shell outside any tab), is not stopped. (C)
3. A finished leaf with no worktree and no leaf temp left but a live tab keeps its slice: the pass fetches the pane list rather than reading an empty one. (B,D)
4. A pass with the pane list unavailable stops no slice of a leaf that has a recorded tab. (B,D)
5. A loaded `akrogon-l*.slice` that matches no leaf record and holds no process and no live run record is stopped. (C)
6. A reconcile pass running inside a leaf slice does not stop that slice.
7. `akrogon phase <slug> merged` stops no slice: its log line and completion run to the end.
8. A guard unit that fails is no longer listed by systemd afterwards.
9. A failed `akrogon-run-*` unit already loaded is no longer listed after a reconcile pass.
/home/ivan/Work/infra/akrogon/issues/open/worktree-cleanup/stacked-member-close/brief.md
# Brief: stacked-member-close

## What
When a stacked merge finishes, the merge path itself closes the tab of every merged member and dispatches each member's dependents, as `closableMembers` did before 6640ab5.

## Why
Tamdoma/akrogon#93 remainder: since 9e4c093 restored stacking without that step, merged members' tabs and worktrees wait on a hook chain that does not always arrive, so their worktrees are kept and their dependents wait.

## Done-criteria
1. After a stacked merge of a holder and two members lands through `akrogon phase <holder> merged`, both member tabs are closed by that command's merge pass without a herdr hook event, and each member's dependent leaves are dispatched.
2. The same holds when the push was first reported failed and a later fetch confirms it landed. (B)
3. The holder's own tab is not closed by this path; it closes on idle as today.
4. A dependent dispatched by this path and again by a later pass is started once.
/home/ivan/Work/infra/akrogon/issues/open/worktree-cleanup/test-isolation/brief.md
# Brief: test-isolation

## What
akrogon's own test suite stops writing into the real home and the real leaf temp root, and ends every process it starts.

## Why
Store-hygiene F1, F4: 35-45 empty repo dirs in `/var/tmp/akr-1000`, an empty `~/.akrogon/worktrees/repo`, and 16 fake seats still sleeping since 2026-10-13 all come from the suite. Cleanup alone would hide a refill.

## Done-criteria
1. A full `bun test` run adds no entry under the real `/var/tmp/akr-<uid>`, `/tmp/akr-<uid>` or `~/.akrogon/worktrees`.
2. After a full `bun test` run exits, no process the suite started is still running.
/home/ivan/Work/infra/akrogon/issues/open/worktree-cleanup/store-sweep/brief.md
# Brief: store-sweep

## What
Every reconcile pass deletes junk in akrogon's own places when ownership proves it safe: unregistered entries in each worktree store and legacy `issues/worktrees` (dangling symlinks and stray files included), finished leaves' temp, dead runs and stray entries in the leaf temp root, the retired `/tmp/akr-<uid>`, store dirs of unregistered repos, retired state and lock files. What it cannot prove safe stays, recorded with the reason and shown by plain status.

## Why
Operator, Round 2 answer 5 and Round 3: akrogon's folders and outputs must always be clean, without breaking anything. About 475 MB of junk sits on this host today (store-hygiene F1), and reconcile cannot see symlinks or stray files.

Builds on three leaves (B,C,D): scratch-copy-removal's process check and `batch-<id>.owner` record, finished-leaf-processes' slice reader and its slice step earlier in the same pass, and kept-status's plain-status kept lines, which host items join.

## Done-criteria
1. In a repo with no running leaf, a reconcile pass deletes: an unregistered folder, a dangling symlink and a stray file in the store and in the legacy root; the temp of a `merged` or `failed` leaf whose tab is gone; a `run-*` dir with a dead owner; a stray file and `.tmp*` dir in the repo's leaf temp; an empty repo dir in the leaf temp root.
2. A host step in the same pass deletes the retired `/tmp/akr-<uid>`, `~/.akrogon/worktrees/<name>` for a name that is no registered repo, a leaf temp repo dir of no registered repo, `runs/last-start`, a `<file>.<pid>.tmp` of a dead pid, and `~/.akrogon/run.lock` and `~/.akrogon/framework-tests.lock` when no process holds them; each repo pass deletes that repo's `.git/akrogon-base-runs.lock` and `issues/.lock` when no process holds them, and its report entries for paths that no longer exist. (C,D)
3. An item tied to a running leaf stays: its temp, a `<slug>-<anything>` store entry, and an unowned entry in that repo.
4. A `run-*` dir or a `batch-<id>.owner` record with a live owner stays in every case, also with no live tab and no running slice for its leaf and when its enclosing folder would otherwise go; a `run-*` dir without `.owner` younger than 60 seconds stays. (B)
5. A `run-*` dir whose owner is dead is deleted while its leaf is still active, also in a pass with the pane list unavailable, as today. (B,C)
6. An item with a live herdr pane inside, or with a process of this user whose cwd or an open file is inside, stays and is recorded with the pane or pid; a pass with the pane list unavailable deletes nothing except a `run-*` dir whose owner is dead. (C)
7. The live locks (`<globalHome>/.lock`, `.git/akrogon-install.lock`, `.git/akrogon-verify-runs.lock`), config, paused and stopped files, `~/.config/akrogon/env`, installed links, `issues/` records and registered worktrees outside the store and legacy root are never deleted.
8. Each kept item appears in `reconcile/<repo>.json`, or `reconcile-host.json` for host items, with its reason and what clears it, and plain `akrogon status` prints host items too, with kept-status's label and placement, also with zero registered repos. (C,D)
9. A delete that fails is reported with its path and error, and no item is reported deleted while it still exists.
10. A pass whose only candidate is a new kind (a dangling symlink, stray file or unknown leaf temp dir) fetches the pane list rather than judging it with an empty one.
